G4715.def:
στατήρ, -ῆρος, ὁ 
[in Aq., Sm., for מִשְׁקָל ;] 
a stater; 
__(a) a weight; 
__(b) a coin (used by late writers of the Greek τετράδραχμον): Matthieu 17:27 26:16, WH, mg.†

G4733.def:
στερέωμα, -τος, τό
(στερεόω), [in LXX: Genèse 1:6 ff., Psaumes 19:1 150:1, Eze.1:22-26 10:1 13:5, Dan LXX, TH Daniel 3:56, Daniel 12:3 (רָקִיעַ), Deutéronome 33:26 (שַׁחַק), Psaumes 18:2 71:3 (סֶלַע), Esther 9:29, I Esther 8:78 (82), Sir.43:1, 8, 1Ma.9:14 * ;] 
a solid body; 
__(a) a support, foundation (Arist., al.); metaphorically, strength (Psaumes 17:1-15 70:1-5, 1Mac, ll. with); steadfastness, firmness: τ. πίστεως, Colossiens 2:5; 
__(b) the dome of heaven (believed to be a solid canopy), the firmament (LXX).†

G4751.def:
στόμαχος, -ου, ὁ
(στόμα), 
prop., a mouth, an opening; 
__(a) in early Gk. writers, the throat; 
__(b) of the opening of the stomach (Arist.); 
__(with) in later writers (Plut., al.), the stomach: 1 Timothée 5:23.†
